    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμ-ωδιάω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>have the teeth set on edge</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				2.55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				886b12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ez.</u>
				18.4
			</span></i> (Cod.A): c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. τοὺς ὀδόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.</u>
					2.73
				</span></i>
			: metaph. of one <i>whose mouth waters</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾑμωδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Timocl.
					11.7
				</span></i>
			. (In this group of words the termination may be connected
			with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδών</span>.)</div>
